  "body": "What happens: `set_tool`, `add_operation` and the UI accept a tool that is too wide for a 2D Pocket. The generator refuses it later with \"pocket is narrower than the tool\". Found during #3475.\n\nWhy #3475 did not fix it: the fit of a pocket depends on the region that the generator cuts. That region depends on the containment (an open side lets a wider tool cut from outside), the stock and the part slice (`operation::selection_region`, `pocket_region_memo`, area controls). The command does not have that region without these steps. A bounding-box or width estimate can refuse legal work, so #3475 added none.\n\nAlso owed (same rule, other doors):\n- `EditOperationParams`: an edit of a plain Slot's `width` or `stock_to_leave` that makes the current tool too wide is not refused at the command. #3475 refuses only at create, at `set_tool` (`EditOperationLinks`) and at a `ChangeTool` that widens the tool. The shared rule is `camcraft_motion::machining2d::slot_centre_band` and the sentence is `operation::tool_gate::slot_fit_refusal`.\n\nExpected: an accepted pocket edit with a named `warning` in the MCP reply (the `clearance_warning` pattern of `edit_operation`), and the same text in the UI, when the generator's own predicate (`non_sliver_center(region, r + stock_to_leave)` is empty) says that the tool cannot fit. The check must use the same region as generate, or it must not run.\n\nDone means: a pinning test shows the warning for a too-wide tool on a closed Inside pocket, and no warning for an Outside pocket that the generator cuts; a Slot width edit below the tool is refused at the command with the #3475 sentence.\n",
